---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Macro Easy - Support"
  description="Need help with Macro Easy?"
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/macro-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Macro Easy?</p>
          <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Macro%20Easy%20Support" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll help with logging, targets, Apple Health or anything else.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I log a meal quickly?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Type it in the field at the bottom of Today with its macros, like “Chicken salad 35p 10c 12f”, and tap the arrow. Check the card that appears and tap Log meal. You can also write “35 g protein” or “protein 35”, and add “yesterday” for a meal you forgot.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I change my targets?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Tap one of the protein, carbs or fat cards on Today, or open the menu, then Settings, then Targets. Calories add up from the three: 4 per gram of protein and carbs, 9 per gram of fat.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do saved meals work?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Turn on Save for later when you log a meal, or touch and hold a meal on Today and choose Save meal. Saved meals sit on Today, in the menu and in search; tap one and then Log meal.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where do food search numbers come from?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">From USDA FoodData Central. Values are per 100 g; pick a serving or type the grams you ate and Macro Easy works out the macros for that amount.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does it work with Apple Health?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes. Open the menu, then Settings, and turn on Save meals to Apple Health. Each meal you log is saved as protein, carbohydrates, total fat and dietary energy. Macro Easy only writes to Apple Health; it never reads from it. If you turned access off, open the Health app, tap your picture, then Apps, Macro Easy.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Will my nutrition data leave my phone?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">No. Meals and targets stay on your iPhone. Food search sends only the words you type, and Apple Health gets your meals only if you turn it on.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
